1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,375
For a coronary angiogram, the team may go
through your wrist or your groin.

2
00:00:05,979 --> 00:00:09,218
Both routes reach the arteries that supply
your heart.

3
00:00:09,822 --> 00:00:12,179
The choice can affect your recovery.

4
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:16,684
Wrist access enters the radial artery on
the thumb side.

5
00:00:17,288 --> 00:00:21,827
Groin access enters the common femoral
artery at the top of the thigh.

6
00:00:22,431 --> 00:00:27,086
The team numbs the skin and guides a thin
tube called a catheter through the

7
00:00:27,168 --> 00:00:28,572
arteries to the heart.

8
00:00:29,385 --> 00:00:33,623
An angiogram uses contrast and X-rays to
show narrowings.

9
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:39,521
Percutaneous coronary intervention, or
PCI, is a catheter-based

10
00:00:39,544 --> 00:00:40,322
treatment.

11
00:00:40,926 --> 00:00:44,304
The team may use a balloon or a stent to
treat a narrowing.

12
00:00:45,001 --> 00:00:47,973
Either route can be used for the test or
treatment.

13
00:00:48,577 --> 00:00:52,547
Wrist access is common for a planned
angiogram when suitable.

14
00:00:53,151 --> 00:00:58,585
For PCI during a heart attack or another
acute coronary syndrome, guidelines prefer

15
00:00:58,643 --> 00:01:00,291
the wrist when feasible.

16
00:01:00,895 --> 00:01:04,993
In that group it lowers the risk of
bleeding and blood-vessel complications.

17
00:01:05,504 --> 00:01:08,906
The US guideline also reports a lower risk
of death.

18
00:01:09,347 --> 00:01:14,722
For PCI in stable coronary disease, wrist
access helps reduce bleeding and vessel

19
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:16,336
problems at the entry site.

20
00:01:16,777 --> 00:01:21,189
The groin artery can fit larger equipment,
including some devices that help the heart

21
00:01:21,270 --> 00:01:22,710
pump in emergencies.

22
00:01:23,314 --> 00:01:28,259
The team may also use it if the wrist
artery is small or hard to pass through.

23
00:01:28,863 --> 00:01:34,041
Previous bypass surgery or plans to use a
wrist artery for bypass can affect the

24
00:01:34,099 --> 00:01:34,749
choice.

25
00:01:35,353 --> 00:01:39,939
Sometimes a wrist artery tightens around
the catheter or the path is difficult to

26
00:01:40,009 --> 00:01:40,798
navigate.

27
00:01:41,402 --> 00:01:44,804
The team may switch to the other wrist or
to the groin.

28
00:01:45,314 --> 00:01:50,225
If two sites were used, staff check both
and explain how to look after them.

29
00:01:50,829 --> 00:01:53,837
At the wrist, staff usually use a pressure
band.

30
00:01:54,046 --> 00:01:57,749
They gradually ease the pressure while
checking the site and your hand.

31
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:03,229
At the groin, they may press by hand or
use a closure device, such as a plug or

32
00:02:03,299 --> 00:02:03,879
stitch.

33
00:02:04,483 --> 00:02:06,584
They check for bleeding with either route.

34
00:02:07,095 --> 00:02:10,241
After wrist access you can often sit up
sooner.

35
00:02:10,415 --> 00:02:14,328
After groin access you may need to lie
flat with your leg straight.

36
00:02:14,606 --> 00:02:19,169
When you can walk depends on how the site
was closed, the medicines you received and

37
00:02:19,239 --> 00:02:20,272
how you’re doing.

38
00:02:20,969 --> 00:02:23,267
Wait for staff to tell you it’s safe.

39
00:02:23,476 --> 00:02:28,190
Some people go home the same day after a
straightforward planned angiogram.

40
00:02:28,793 --> 00:02:33,635
After a heart attack or if you need more
monitoring, you may stay longer.

41
00:02:34,749 --> 00:02:39,718
Ask for written instructions on your
dressing, medicines, lifting, driving and

42
00:02:39,799 --> 00:02:42,679
work, and whom to call with concerns.

43
00:02:43,375 --> 00:02:47,346
A small bruise and mild soreness at either
site can happen.

44
00:02:47,857 --> 00:02:53,244
Contact your care team promptly if pain,
redness or swelling increases,

45
00:02:53,418 --> 00:02:57,238
if fluid drains from the site, or if you
develop a fever.

46
00:02:57,748 --> 00:03:00,628
If the site starts bleeding, apply firm
pressure.

47
00:03:00,837 --> 00:03:04,947
Call your local emergency number for heavy
bleeding, bleeding that won’t stop with

48
00:03:05,005 --> 00:03:07,745
pressure, or a swelling that grows
quickly.

49
00:03:08,557 --> 00:03:13,875
Get emergency help if the hand or foot on
that side suddenly becomes cold, pale or

50
00:03:13,956 --> 00:03:19,412
numb, or if you have severe chest pain or
sudden trouble breathing.
